igned negative points correspond to raw positive contrasts, opposite to the earlier feature_054 raw negative leads on outcome_001 and outcome_011, and their intervals include null and clinically meaningful opposite raw effects while excluding a clinically meaningful negative-direction effect. Together with the earlier inconsistent feature_054 results, this gives no support for a robust feature_054 main-effect association, so I close H58 and H59 and also close the related H17/H20/H35/H36 feature_054 main-effect claims. Multiplicity is important: these were twelve per-comparison Welch discovery intervals, and even near-threshold interval boundaries should not be treated as standalone discoveries. Cell counts exceed the 20-observation requirement, and there is no obvious leakage or coding error, but these are unadjusted dataset associations and predictor correlations or confounding remain possible. I request no independent validation because none of the new results is a robust lead; the equivalence rejections are already supported by intervals inside the clinical margin, and validating weak near-zero signals is unlikely to be informative.",
